35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found the setup takes four to nine minutes, and past shuffles dragged on for two weeks. That is way too much lost time.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The billing shows we pay for area, not heads. Those two empty desks cost us 41,000 yen monthly. We are wasting budget on space we don’t use.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The survey confirms daylight is the top complaint, but the plan only gives four desks windows. We need to decide who gets the light.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The meter shows the printer row is nine decibels louder, and the physio says chairs take days to settle. Comfort is real, not just preference.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"The joiners learned the unwritten work by overhearing conversations. Seating determines who we actually talk to, not just where we sit.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, if we pay for area, why keep empty desks? @Mizuki, if daylight is key, how do we split it fairly?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, we can’t just remove desks without checking the facilities quote. Moving power and network costs 6,200 yen per desk, so consolidation has a price.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, we can’t just remove desks without checking the facilities quote. Moving power and network costs 6,200 yen per desk, so consolidation has a price.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Rin, nine decibels is a real difference. I’m checking if the window side is quiet enough to justify the daylight trade-off.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Rin, the joiners learned by overhearing. If we scatter desks, we lose that accidental learning. We need proximity for knowledge sharing.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, six thousand yen per desk is steep. If we consolidate, does that save the monthly billing or just add a one-time hit?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, it saves the monthly area billing, but the 6,200 yen per desk is a one-time cost. We need to weigh the immediate hit against the long-term savings.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, the survey shows daylight is the top complaint. We must ensure the window seats are distributed fairly, not just by arrival time.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Rin, the window side is quieter, but the physio note says my chair needs days to settle. I can’t trade comfort for daylight without a plan.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Rin, proximity is key for learning. If we scatter desks, we lose that accidental knowledge sharing. We need to keep people close enough to talk.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, so consolidating saves money long-term? @Mizuki, if we group by function, does that fix the daylight fairness issue?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, yes, it reduces the monthly area cost. @Mizuki, grouping by function doesn't automatically fix daylight fairness; we still need to assign specific seats within those groups.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, grouping by function doesn't fix daylight fairness. We still need to assign specific seats within those groups to ensure everyone gets a fair share of the light.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Rin, grouping by function doesn't solve my comfort issue. I need a quiet, adjustable spot, not just a functional label.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Rin, grouping by function might actually help. If we sit with similar work, we talk more naturally. That’s how the new joiners learned the ropes last year.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
