60,3,1,talk,Rin,,I need to know the options. How do we handle the setup time and the daylight split in each one?,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, the options are A: Free Address, B: Rotating Blocks, C: Fixed Desks by Function. I need to see which minimizes the 6,200 yen re-run costs.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, option C seems best for fairness. If seats are fixed and named, we can deliberately assign the window desks to rotate or balance the load, rather than letting habit decide.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, fixed seats mean I can finally settle my chair and monitor arms. Rotating blocks would force me to re-adjust my setup every few months, which the physio says takes days.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, fixed seats by function actually help me. If we sit with similar work, we talk more naturally. That’s how the new joiners learned the ropes last year.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, if C is fixed, does that mean I keep my desk? I hate the four-to-nine minute setup every morning.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, yes, C means a permanent seat. You avoid the daily setup cost, but you pay the 6,200 yen re-run fee once to move it.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, yes, C means a permanent seat. You avoid the daily setup cost, but you pay the 6,200 yen re-run fee once to move it.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Rin, yes, C means a permanent seat. You avoid the daily setup cost, but you pay the 6,200 yen re-run fee once to move it.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Rin, yes, C means a permanent seat. You avoid the daily setup cost, but you pay the 6,200 yen re-run fee once to move it.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, so C saves my morning gaps? @Mizuki, if seats are fixed, how do we ensure the window desks aren't just hoarded by the early birds?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, yes, C saves your morning gaps. @Mizuki, fixed seats prevent hoarding because assignments are deliberate, not first-come. We decide who gets the light, not the badge scanner.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, exactly. Fixed assignments mean we decide who gets the light, not the badge scanner. We can balance the window seats deliberately, rather than letting habit or arrival time decide.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, fixed seats also lock in the quiet. I can finally settle my chair without the printer row noise. That is the comfort I need.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, fixed seats by function mean I sit with similar work. That’s how the new joiners learned the ropes. It buys us natural conversation, not just furniture.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, if C is fixed, does that mean I keep my desk? I hate the four-to-nine minute setup every morning.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, yes, C is a permanent seat. You avoid the daily setup cost, but you pay the 6,200 yen re-run fee once to move it.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
